{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-self-dual-2group","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:self-dual-2group","kind":"remark","title":"Self-duality as constrained 2-group gauge theory","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-instanton"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-self-duality","tags":["2-group","gauge-theory","instanton"],"text":"self-dual-2group.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:self-dual-2group\"></a><p>A <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-connection for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{INN}(G)</code> dictates <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A = B</code>. Under the simplicity constraint <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B \\in \\Gamma(\\Lambda^+\\!H^* \\otimes \\mathrm{Ad}(P))</code>, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-form datum is self-dual. The conjunction of quantum flatness <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A = B</code> and simplicity forces <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A = F_A^+</code>, securing the instanton equation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A^- = 0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/self-dual-2group.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.25.6"}
